  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Eswatini Green Finance Taxonomy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Eswatini Green Finance Taxonomy project aims to operationalize a national framework that classifies and guides sustainable investments. Anchored under UNDP&#x2019;s &#x201c;Central Bank of Eswatini Green Bonds&#x201d; initiative, the taxonomy provides clear standards for identifying, tracking, and reporting green finance activities. By establishing transparent criteria, it strengthens investor confidence, promotes issuance of green bonds, and ensures alignment with international best practices in climate finance.This project is a cornerstone in Eswatini&#x2019;s transition toward a sustainable economy, mobilizing resources for climate-resilient development, enhancing accountability in financial markets, and positioning the country as a regional leader in green finance innovation.</narrative>
  </description>
